-- title:
--   Evaluation at places commutes with coefficientwise constant extension
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $K'$ be fields equipped with $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra structures, let $\sigma\colon K \to K'$ be a ring homomorphism, and let $F_0$ be an intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q} \subseteq \mathbb{Q}(\!(q)\!)$. For a field $L$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ write $L\!\cdot\!F_0 =$ `laurentBaseChange L F₀` for the intermediate field of $L(\!(q)\!)$ generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise images of $F_0$ under $\mathbb{Q} \to L$. Let $v$ be a place of $K\!\cdot\!F_0$ over $K$ and $w$ a place of $K'\!\cdot\!F_0$ over $K'$, each being a proper valuation subring containing the image of the base field and whose ring of integers is a principal ideal ring. Assume the compatibility: for all $x \in K\!\cdot\!F_0$ and $x' \in K'\!\cdot\!F_0$ whose underlying Laurent series satisfy $x' = \mathrm{coeffMap}\,\sigma\,(x)$, one has $\mathrm{ord}_w(x') = \mathrm{ord}_v(x)$, where $\mathrm{ord}$ denotes minus the logarithm of the associated adic valuation. Assume further that $v$ is rational, i.e. $K \to$ (residue field of $v$) is surjective. Then for $x$ lying in the valuation subring of $v$ and $x'$ with $x' = \mathrm{coeffMap}\,\sigma\,(x)$ coefficientwise, the residue value of $x'$ at $w$ equals $\sigma$ applied to the residue value of $x$ at $v$, values being taken via the chosen inverse of the residue map along the base field (and set to $0$ outside the valuation subring). Rationality of $w$ is not assumed.
--
--   This is the statement that evaluation of a function at a rational place commutes with extension of the constant field, in the concrete setting of subfields of Laurent series generated by $q$-expansions: with $F_0$ the field of $q$-expansions of modular functions for $\Gamma_0(N)$ it compares values of a modular function at an algebraic point with values of its $\sigma$-image at the corresponding complex point. It is used in the treatment of specialisations of $j$- and $H$-type places, for instance in the computations of denominators for inertia-stable annulus data and in the compatibility of evaluation with the arithmetic Galois action.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_evalAt_eq_apply_evalAt_of_coe_eq_coeffMap.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_PlaceEvaluation

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

open AlgebraicCurve ModularCurve

theorem ModularCurve.evalAt_eq_apply_evalAt_of_coe_eq_coeffMap {K K' : Type*} [Field K] [Field K']
    [Algebra ℚ K] [Algebra ℚ K'] (σ : K →+* K') (F₀ : IntermediateField ℚ (LaurentSeries ℚ))
    (v : Place K (laurentBaseChange K F₀)) (w : Place K' (laurentBaseChange K' F₀))
    (hw : ∀ (x : laurentBaseChange K F₀) (x' : laurentBaseChange K' F₀),
      (x' : LaurentSeries K') = coeffMap σ (x : LaurentSeries K) → w.ord x' = v.ord x)
    (hv : v.IsRational)
    (x : laurentBaseChange K F₀) (x' : laurentBaseChange K' F₀)
    (hx' : (x' : LaurentSeries K') = coeffMap σ (x : LaurentSeries K)) (hx : x ∈ v.toValuationSubring) :
    w.evalAt x' = σ (v.evalAt x) := by sorry
